(N.D.A.C. 75-02-01.2-85 )

All referred individuals are required to participate in one or more work activities for periods of time necessary to allow a participant to complete tasks that will move them directly into employment.

Following are the allowable work activities within the JOBS program:

Unsubsidized Employment;

Subsidized public or private sector employment

On the Job Training;

Public or private work experience;

Job Search and job readiness activities;

Community Service;

Vocational Training;

Education directly related to employment for a participant under age 20 who has not completed high school or received a GED ;

Satisfactory attendance at secondary school or in a course of study leading to a GED for a participate under age 20;

Providing child care services to another participant engaged in a community service program; and

Job skills training directly related to employment.

(Revised 9/1/2021 ML #3629)

